 "relevance_note": "In a 1000-patient genomic diagnostics cohort, the supplementary variant table (Additional file 1 excerpt) gives one patient row with a TNFAIP3 variant, \"<em>TNFAIP3</em> (NM_001270508.1): c.1939A&gt;C; p.(Thr647Pro)\", with test type and ACMG codes, which is individual-level detail; the main text does not mention TNFAIP3.",
 "method_note": "Read the whole paper by hand; no script transcribed values (a script only assembled the JSON and checked spans/fields). TNFAIP3 appears only in the Supplementary material excerpt of Additional file 1 (lines mentioning TNFAIP3 with 3 lines of context; omitted text marked [...]). Two TNFAIP3 mentions: (a) a disease-count table row '<td><em>TNFAIP3</em></td> / <td>Autoinflammatory syndrome, familial, Behcet-like</td> / <td>1</td>'; (b) one variant-table row with cells 'AD' (colspan=2), 'Indication based Exome', the variant, 'PS3, PP3, PP4', '6:138201240', 'Novel'. The excerpt does not show the variant row's case number, table number or column headers, so the label rules 1 and 3 cannot be applied; the person is labelled 'unnamed person 1' (rule 6). One person recorded: the variant row. The count table (a) is not treated as a separate person; it is likely the same patient but the excerpt does not link the disease label to the variant row explicitly, so disease_label_as_stated is 'not reported' (candidate label: 'Autoinflammatory syndrome, familial, Behcet-like'). The supplement is raw HTML: the Markdown prints '&gt;' for '>'. Spans copy '&gt;' literally; values give the decoded form 'c.1939A>C'. 'AD' (column header not shown, probably mode of inheritance) was not converted to zygosity or inheritance (rule 8); 'Novel' (probably novel vs previously reported) was not recorded as a pathogenicity classification; no pathogenicity class (P/LP/VUS) is printed for this row. PS3 is recorded only as an ACMG code; no functional assay result is described. No genome build is printed for '6:138201240'. is_proband left null: the main text calls all 1000 patients 'probands' ('Of the 1000 probands'), but the excerpt row itself carries no proband statement. n_patients_reported null: the authors do not state a number of TNFAIP3 patients in the text (the count table gives 1 for the TNFAIP3 disease entry). No sex, age, ancestry, consanguinity, phenotype or treatment is shown for this person, so phenotypic_features is empty and all 20 checklist items are 'not reported'. Out of scope: the other cohort patients, including case 297 (DOCK8). No contradictions found.",
